Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild RTSP audio subsession on live audio codec/rate change
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable).
Stacks on: 0001-0013. Applies with git apply -p1 / patch -p1 AFTER them.

Changing the audio codec (mic_format: OPUS<->AAC<->...) or the input sample
rate (mic_sample_rate) live via the web UI / JsonAPI stuttered AAC horribly and
killed go2rtc audio on AAC->OPUS, recoverable only by `S31prudynt restart`.

ROOT CAUSE (source-verified). handle_audio raised global_restart_audio ONLY for
mic_format / mic_sample_rate, never global_restart_rtsp. In main()'s supervisor
loop global_restart_audio DOES join+respawn the AudioWorker (thread_entry ->
IMPAudio::createNew re-reads cfg->audio.input_format), so the encoder rebuilds
and real new-codec bytes hit the wire. But only global_restart_rtsp re-runs
RTSP::start(), the sole path that rebuilds ServerMediaSession, the
IMPAudioServerMediaSubsession, the audio IMPDeviceSource and the persistent
StreamReplicator -- and thereby regenerates the audio SDP. live555 freezes the
subsession's fSDPLines at the first DESCRIBE (IMPAudioServerMediaSubsession
overrides neither sdpLines() nor getAuxSDPLine()), so a client (go2rtc) that
negotiated once keeps depacketizing against the old codec's rtpmap/clock/payload
type. New AAC bytes vs the stale negotiated SDP -> clock/framing skew (stutter);
AAC->OPUS (SimpleRTPSink, clock forced 48000, 2ch, dynamic PT) is unmappable to
a session holding AAC MPEG4-GENERIC -> audio drops entirely; video is a separate
subsession so it survives. A full restart rebuilt encoder + RTSP + SDP together,
which is why it worked.

FIX. On a REAL change to an SDP-affecting audio key, raise global_restart_rtsp
in addition to global_restart_audio -- the exact discipline 0001/0004 use for the
video "format" key. In main()'s restart loop audio is (re)started BEFORE rtsp, so
the new audioSource/StreamReplicator (RTSP::start) bind the respawned worker's
PERSISTENT global_audio[0]->msgChannel (allocated once in main, never recreated)
so there is no starvation, unlike the 0007 bare-global_restart_audio (input
disabled) case. The new IMPAudioServerMediaSubsession computes a fresh SDP and go2rtc
re-DESCRIBEs against the true codec on reconnect.

Stock handle_audio raises the restart flag UNCONDITIONALLY on key presence (no
diff-check -- the cfg->set<>() return is ignored), so this patch adds a read-back
diff-gate (rebuild only when old != new) so HA/agent state re-sends do not
needlessly churn the RTSP server (which also briefly reconnects video, since one
RTSP thread serves both subsessions).

SDP-affecting keys handled: mic_format (codec) and mic_sample_rate (RTP clock for
non-OPUS codecs; OPUS forces 48000 regardless). force_stereo (channel count) is a
related candidate left untouched for now (separate, rarer live toggle).

diff --git a/src/JsonAPI.cpp b/src/JsonAPI.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/JsonAPI.cpp
+++ b/src/JsonAPI.cpp
@@ -762,6 +762,44 @@ void handle_audio(JsonValue *obj, std::string &out, bool &sep) {
   // Input
   add_boolk_a("mic_enabled", "audio.mic_enabled", false, true);
-  add_strk_a("mic_format", "audio.mic_format", true);
+  // mic_format / mic_sample_rate are SDP-affecting (codec and RTP clock). On a
+  // REAL change they must rebuild the RTSP audio subsession too, so its cached
+  // SDP is regenerated and clients (go2rtc) re-DESCRIBE against the new codec.
+  // global_restart_audio alone respawns the encoder (new bytes on the wire) but
+  // leaves the stale SDP -> AAC stutters, AAC->OPUS drops audio. Mirrors the
+  // video "format" path; diff-gated (read-back) so HA/agent re-sends never churn.
+  auto add_strk_a_rtsp = [&](const char *key, const char *path) {
+    if (JsonValue *v = obj_get(obj, key)) {
+      if (v->type == JSON_STRING && v->value.string) {
+        const char *oldv = cfg->get<const char *>(path);
+        bool changed = !oldv || strcmp(oldv, v->value.string) != 0;
+        cfg->set<const char *>(path, strdup(v->value.string));
+        if (changed) {
+          global_restart_audio = true;
+          global_restart_rtsp = true;
+        }
+      }
+      add_key(out, s2, key);
+      add_str(out, cfg->get<const char *>(path));
+      wrote = true;
+    }
+  };
+  auto add_int_a_rtsp = [&](const char *key, const char *path) {
+    if (JsonValue *v = obj_get(obj, key)) {
+      if (v->type == JSON_NUMBER) {
+        int newv = (int)v->value.number.integer;
+        bool changed = cfg->get<int>(path) != newv;
+        cfg->set<int>(path, newv);
+        if (changed) {
+          global_restart_audio = true;
+          global_restart_rtsp = true;
+        }
+      }
+      add_key(out, s2, key);
+      add_num(out, cfg->get<int>(path));
+      wrote = true;
+    }
+  };
+  add_strk_a_rtsp("mic_format", "audio.mic_format");

   // mic_vol - apply immediately without restart
   if (JsonValue *v = obj_get(obj, "mic_vol")) {
@@ -800,4 +800,4 @@ void handle_audio(JsonValue *obj, std::string &out, bool &sep) {
   }
   add_int("mic_bitrate", "audio.mic_bitrate", true);
-  add_int("mic_sample_rate", "audio.mic_sample_rate", true);
+  add_int_a_rtsp("mic_sample_rate", "audio.mic_sample_rate");
 #if defined(LIB_AUDIO_PROCESSING)
